{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ENfEKifaZMj847u4MMqN4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# vNEXT — Title (one line, what this release does)\n2\t\n3\t<!-- Copy to releases/_next/<slug>.md. Do NOT pick a version number and do NOT\n4\t     touch VERSION — release.yml assigns the number at merge and replaces\n5\t     \"vNEXT\" in the heading. Keep \"vNEXT\" literally as written. -->\n6\t\n7\t**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD\n8\t**PR:** #N\n9\t**Type:** patch\n10\t\n11\t<!-- Type must be exactly one of: patch | minor | major (CI enforces this).\n12\t     It drives the version bump at merge. -->\n13\t\n14\t## Summary\n15\t\n16\t[What changed and why — three sentences max.]\n17\t\n18\t## Changes\n19\t\n20\t- [The bullet list a future reader greps.]\n21\t\n22\t## Local deployment\n23\t\n24\t[Ordered, copy-pasteable commands for the Mac. \"Nothing to do.\" if true —\n25\tnever omit this section; CI checks for it.]\n26\t\n27\t## Manual steps\n28\t\n29\t[One-off human actions after merge that no command covers: repo settings,\n30\texternal platforms, account consoles. Say where, what to change, and to\n31\twhat. \"Nothing to do.\" if none — never omit this section; CI checks for it.]\n32\t\n33\t## Verification\n34\t\n35\t[Copy-pasteable commands proving the change is live, run against main AFTER\n36\tmerge. At least one bash block (CI enforces it). Commands only — no comment\n37\tlines, no trailing # comments: a pasted block must run as-is. State each\n38\tcheck's expected output in prose after the block.]\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\tgit checkout main && git pull\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\t[Expected: ...]\n45\t\n46\t## Rollback\n47\t\n48\t[How to get back — usually git checkout of the previous tag, plus any\n49\tlaunchctl bootout/bootstrap to reverse.]\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"908c0fb5-3108-4d6f-a1a1-3f2f79af6fb0","uuid":"58649af4-dbad-490c-8b22-6a4dee57f932","timestamp":"2026-10-07T22:30:14.571Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text",