{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfofha6uMWZEK8TFkXuMn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Wr8LD3ZemnNSFMV459q3z","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md","content":"# vNEXT — The test suite no longer writes to logs/usage/\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-08\n**PR:** #TBD\n**Type:** patch\n\n## Summary\n\nRunning the test suite used to append `function:*` test records to `logs/usage/`. A session-wide guard in `tests/conftest.py` now fails any test that would write there (ADR-021), and the tests that record usage do so in a temporary directory. Only tests and release notes changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `tests/conftest.py`: guard around `harness.usage.append_jsonl` that fails with the target directory in the message, plus a `usage_log_dir` fixture.\n- `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py`: shows the guard stopping a write, with positive controls.\n- Legacy tool-loop test modules and the live tier opt into `usage_log_dir`.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main && git pull\n(find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} + 2>/dev/null; ls logs/usage 2>/dev/null) > /tmp/usage_before.txt\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n(find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} + 2>/dev/null; ls logs/usage 2>/dev/null) > /tmp/usage_after.txt\ndiff /tmp/usage_before.txt /tmp/usage_after.txt && echo UNCHANGED\n```\n\nExpected: the suite passes and the last line printed is `UNCHANGED`, meaning the line counts and file names under `logs/usage/` are the same before and after.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`git revert` the merge commit. No data or deployment state is involved. Files already in `logs/usage/` are not touched by this change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2652,"cache_read_input_tokens":31368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2652},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"908c0fb5-3108-4d6f-a1a1-3f2f79af6fb0","uuid":"4d377046-d304-4332-9339-6f26b8f24793","timestamp":"2026-10-07T22:30:19.528Z","request_id":"req_011CfofhZir1L3RTmhBAjyjz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016Wr8LD3ZemnNSFMV459q3z":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md","content":"# vNEXT — The test suite no longer writes to logs/usage/\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-08\n**PR:** #TBD\n**Type:** patch\n\n## Summary\n\nRunning the test suite used to append `function:*` test records to `logs/usage/`. A session-wide guard in `tests/conftest.py` now fails any test that would write there (ADR-021), and the tests that record usage do so in a temporary directory. Only tests and release notes changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `tests/conftest.py`: guard around `harness.usage.append_jsonl` that fails with the target directory in the message, plus a `usage_log_dir` fixture.\n- `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py`: shows the guard stopping a write, with positive controls.\n- Legacy tool-loop test modules and the live tier opt into `usage_log_dir`.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main && git pull\n(find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} + 2>/dev/null; ls logs/usage 2>/dev/null) > /tmp/usage_before.txt\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n(find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} + 2>/dev/null; ls logs/usage 2>/dev/null) > /tmp/usage_after.txt\ndiff /tmp/usage_before.txt /tmp/usage_after.txt && echo UNCHANGED\n```\n\nExpected: the suite passes and the last line printed is `UNCHANGED`, meaning the line counts and file names under `logs/usage/` are the same before and after.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`git revert` the merge commit. No data or deployment state is involved. Files already in `logs/usage/` are not touched by this change.\n"}}}
